{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Lk8iqQhVEVYcRLUSbgkaC8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/02-005-design-a-generative-qa-assistant-for-your-companys-knowledge.md`** — Q5: *Design a generative QA assistant for your company's knowledge base.*\n\nKey content in the note:\n- **4-phase architecture**: source connectors (Confluence/Notion/Drive/Slack/GitHub) → ACL-aware hybrid ingestion → retrieval (dense + BM25 + RRF + cross-encoder rerank) → grounded generation at T=0 with inline citations\n- **ACL enforcement**: user group metadata extracted at ingest, applied as a hard filter before every vector query — explicitly called out as a P0 concern most candidates miss\n- **Freshness strategy**: polling vs webhook-triggered incremental re-embedding tradeoff (80% cost reduction with webhooks)\n- **Model tiering**: GPT-4o-mini for simple factual queries (~$0.0005/query), GPT-4o for complex synthesis; routing on reranker confidence + context length\n- **Eval framework**: RAGAS faithfulness ≥ 0.85, context recall ≥ 0.80 on a 100-pair golden dataset; deflection rate < 10% in production as retrieval health signal\n- **4 pitfalls**: missing ACL enforcement, ignoring freshness/stale indexes, substituting thumbs-up for structured eval, ignoring format heterogeneity (PDFs + Confluence + Slack + code)\n\n30 tasks remaining in the Next queue."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":58688,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":392,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a06487b1-50b3-458f-b738-522ded1339c3","uuid":"5ee60087-d994-42e4-b48c-568c9933c45e"}
